A||||11||FieroLisa||Muffler Shop Install/Spin Tech??? Help!!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||11-17-2001||03:13 PM||||Here's the deal. I bought a Spintech muffler from West Coast Fiero which was advertised as having a factory fit. So today I take my car to "beanys mufflerland" and ask them for an estimate. They proceed to tell me that there is no way it is a direct fit and it will take 5-6 hours labor, take the whole exhaust down and they will need to replace my tail pipes and they can't guarantee anything.<BR>This doesn't seem quite right to me- so has anyone used a Spintech and had it installed sucessfully for less than my estimated $350?? <BR>The shop also tried to tell me that just installing a normal Fiero muffler would cost something like $150 because they would have to replace the tail pipes with that too.<BR>Is this shop screwing me or what?!?! Arg, I'm mad. Advice Please!!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-17-2001||03:30 PM||||Not wanting to sound fresh or anything, but they saw you coming!<BR>Sounds like a bent over type screwing! Even the estimate is wrong, unless the are trying to piece something together? Even then, it wouldn't look good and would leak all over!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jim Keyton||11-17-2001||05:24 PM||||That's way out of line. Had my Spintech installed this spring for $160, and that included $120 worth of tips. They necked down the stock exhaust pipe to fit the muffler and then made up two new exits to the tips.<BR>The shop I used was a small owner owned operation. May want to check with some the hot rodders in your local area.<BR>Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||11-17-2001||05:30 PM||||Or take a guy with you to pretend the car is his. That way they won't try to rip him off, because he is a guy and "knows" cars. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||11-17-2001||06:36 PM||||Well the dumb thing about it, is these people gave me a half way decent price to install my tips- and they know I know cars... and I DID have a guy with me today. So screw them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> They made it seem like such a huge deal that the stock pipes are 2 inch and the muffler has that 2.5 inch. <BR>So I guess I should look around till I find a place that is under $100? At least I have until March, so no hurries  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ...I just wanted to make sure that this spintech really IS as factory fit as advertised. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||11-17-2001||06:40 PM||||Yeah, take it some place else.  They sound like they're taking advantage with the old "It's alot of work" routine.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bruce||11-17-2001||11:10 PM||||Why not just exchange it for West Coast's Flowmaster muffler, which is a direct connect. I paid $45 to have mine installed, and I really like it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||12:05 AM||||I used to manage a muffler shop and it sounds to me like they just didn't want the job. We specialized in custom exhaust and just to make your 2" tailpipes fit the 2 1/4" muffler outlets is no big deal. I agree, look for someplace that will do it for less than $100. That sounds like a fair price.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||8
Z||000008||VeeSixGeeTee||11-18-2001||12:08 AM||||I agree, sounds like they don't want to work on your machine!...I personaly think that Fiero exhaust is very easy to work on.  I'd try a little family owned shop.<P>------------------<BR>Mikey<BR>85 GT 4sp..Taking a six month nap!<BR>AIM: KilleredGT||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||11-18-2001||09:19 PM||||Personally that sounds like a screw job.  And I would never run a spin trap anyway. Now a flowmaster, thats a different story.||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||11-18-2001||09:25 PM||||Lisa, they're trying to pull one over on ya.  Sheah, AS IF you wouldn't notice! ;)<P>Definately go somewhere else, adapting pipe sizes is super-easy (a $2 bent metal piece that they've got a box full of and they're done.)<P>Can't wait to hear what the Spin Tech sounds like!!! (hey, can't at least one of your ex-s handle a welder? what's the world coming to when a girl has to weld her own pipes!? ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||Formula88||11-18-2001||11:03 PM||||Hey, Lisa, is there a 2" SpinTech available, or does it only come with the 2.5" inlet/outlets?  <P>I'm wanting to do this swap, but I was planning on getting their entire 2.5" exhaust piping, too.  But, if they have a SpinTech with the 2" inlet/outlets, it should be plug and play, assuming the physical size is comparable.<P>Bring the Fiero down to NC in Dec. and I'll take you to the muffler shop that welded up the exhaust I got from Hoop.  They did a good job and it was pretty cheap.  He even knew Fiero's used stainless steel exhaust.  I watched him build a custom dual exhaust for a 66 Mustang while I was there, and the man does good work.  He'll be getting my business when I get ready to install the new exhaust on my car next Spring.  ||||reg||6
